WEBVTT - Le Sablier, intro EN (recalé sur la VO définitive)

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.422 line:-4
There are cities built on stone.
Bab El is built on time.

00:00:06.502 --> 00:00:13.210 line:-4
Nine tiers of copper and limestone,
raised around a portal that never opened.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.336 line:-4
And beneath it…
a desert that rises.

00:00:17.366 --> 00:00:20.251 line:-4
Above the ninth tier turns the Astrolabe.

00:00:20.331 --> 00:00:24.735 line:-4
It does not count the hours.
It counts the cycles we have left.

00:00:24.815 --> 00:00:26.037 line:-4
And when it tolls…

00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:32.168 line:-4
The first tier is already lost.
Then the second. Then the third.

00:00:32.248 --> 00:00:38.120 line:-4
Today, we live on the fourth.
Everyone knows. And everyone keeps living.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.769 line:-4
What holds the city together is no king, no god.

00:00:42.849 --> 00:00:46.457 line:-4
It is an administration: the Chamber of Hours.

00:00:46.537 --> 00:00:52.391 line:-4
Every cycle, it publishes the List —
those evacuated first… and the others.

00:00:52.471 --> 00:00:56.160 line:-4
Its agents carry no weapons.
They carry ledgers.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:02.244 line:-4
Here, sand does not fall from the sky —
it rises from the ground.

00:01:02.324 --> 00:01:06.206 line:-4
And it keeps the trace.
Where someone has fallen,

00:01:06.286 --> 00:01:09.509 line:-4
the sand keeps their weight as a hollow.

00:01:09.589 --> 00:01:15.287 line:-4
The poor sell sand heavy with memories.
The rich pay to have it sifted.

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:18.590 line:-4
Nothing that falls is lost… to everyone.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:25.545 line:-4
Salem goes down into the condemned tiers
before the taking, to make sure no one is left.

00:01:25.625 --> 00:01:27.526 line:-4
Hooked pole, rope, notebook.

00:01:27.606 --> 00:01:31.275 line:-4
He always brings someone back.
And it is never enough.

00:01:32.155 --> 00:01:36.758 line:-4
At his side: Yamina, the clockmaker,
who signed a List at nineteen —

00:01:36.838 --> 00:01:40.672 line:-4
and has been trying to repair
the irreparable ever since.

00:01:40.752 --> 00:01:44.307 line:-4
Fériel, the glassblower,
who turns sand into shields.

00:01:44.387 --> 00:01:50.457 line:-4
Boualem, the well-digger, who found something
beneath the city… and does not speak of it.

00:01:50.537 --> 00:01:55.559 line:-4
And Tarek, the porter, who carries
the Chamber's crates — and its secrets.

00:01:56.439 --> 00:02:03.282 line:-4
This time, Salem came back up with twelve people
from a condemned district. Twelve living souls.

00:02:03.862 --> 00:02:06.081 line:-4
— They're standing right behind me.

00:02:06.761 --> 00:02:10.730 line:-4
— I'm not asking where they are.
I'm asking where they are written.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:16.764 line:-4
The district has been officially empty since yesterday.

00:02:16.844 --> 00:02:20.579 line:-4
With no registration, no shelter in the upper tiers.

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:23.440 line:-4
Twelve living souls… who exist nowhere.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:30.710 line:-4
One recourse remains. An old right,
one even the Chamber honours: trial by duel.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.396 line:-4
The cards are fragments of memory, and pacts.

00:02:34.476 --> 00:02:39.392 line:-4
A keeper who loses must open their archives…
or grant passage.

00:02:39.472 --> 00:02:42.996 line:-4
So we will fight. Not to kill.
To be written.

00:02:43.876 --> 00:02:49.251 line:-4
At the top of the Tower of Lists
waits the Grand Horologist Mahieddine.

00:02:49.331 --> 00:02:56.031 line:-4
A gentle man, polite, who offers you tea…
and has been signing the List for forty years.

00:02:56.111 --> 00:02:57.122 line:-4
He never lies.

00:02:57.202 --> 00:02:57.823 line:-4
He omits.

00:02:59.453 --> 00:03:02.760 line:-4
And behind it all, the sealed portal.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:08.068 line:-4
No one knows who built it.
No one knows what it holds back.

00:03:08.148 --> 00:03:12.461 line:-4
But the Astrolabe will toll again.
And this time…

00:03:15.141 --> 00:03:17.020 line:-4
…you hold the cards.
